ot for use in diagnostic procedures.\nL121: \nL122: Specifications\nL123: \nL124: Chemical Reactivity Amine\nL125: \nL126: Label or Dye QSY™ 9\nL127: \nL128: Product Type Succinimidyl Ester\nL129: \nL130: Quantity 5 mg\nL131: \nL132: Reactive Moiety Active Ester, Succinimidyl Ester\nL133: \nL134: Shipping Condition Room Temperature\nL135: \nL136: Label Type Quencher Dyes\nL137: \nL138: Product Line QSY\nL139: \nL140: Unit Size Each\nL141: \nL142: Contents & Storage\nL143: \nL144: Store in freezer (-5 to -30°C) and protect from light.\nL145: ## Citations & References (1)\nL146: \nL147: Citations & References\nL148: \nL149: Abstract\nL150: \nL151: Actin filament uncapping localizes to ruffling lamellae and rocketing vesicles.\nL152: \nL153: Authors:Allen PG\nL154: \nL155: Journal:Nat Cell Biol\nL156: \nL157: PubMed ID:14557819\nL158: Regulated actin filament assembly is critical for eukaryotic cell physiology. Actin filaments are polar structures, and those with free high affinity or barbed ends are crucial for actin dynamics and cell motility. Actin filament barbed-end-capping proteins inhibit filament elongation after binding, and their regulated disassociation is proposed to provide a ... More\nL159: \nL160: Ordering\nL161: \nL162:   * 【52†Order Status】\nL163:   * 【56†Order Help】\nL164:   * 【51†Quick Order】\nL165:   * 【57†Supply Center】\nL166:   * 【58†eProcurement】\nL167: \nL168: Support\nL169:   * 【59†Help and Support】\nL170:   * 【50†Contact Us】\nL171:   * 【60†Technical Support Centers】\nL172:   * 【61†Documents and Certificates】\nL173:   * Report a Site Issue\nL174: \nL175: Resources\nL176: \nL177:   * 【62†Learning Centers】\nL178:   * 【63†Promotions】\nL179:   * 【64†Events and Webinars】\nL180:   * 【65†Social Media】\nL181: \nL182: About Thermo Fisher\nL183:   * 【66†About Us†corporate.thermofisher.com】\nL184:   * 【67†Careers†jobs.thermofisher.com】\nL185:   * 【68†Investors†ir.thermofisher.com】\nL186:   * 【69†News†thermofisher.mediaroom.com】\nL187:   * 【70†Social Respo